# BodyCombat program builder

## Scope

- Assemble a 30, 45, or 60 minute BodyCombat class from the embedded track
  catalog. Follow the fixed track order for that duration and keep the total
  inside the selected time.
- Do not add workout coaching, calorie targets, or training plans.
- Keep this tool independent from the Parcel demo (`src/index3.js`), news
  (`src/news/**`), kakeibo (`src/kakeibo/**`), and receipts (`src/receipts/**`).

## Catalog

- Track titles and artists come from https://www.fhstr.net/archives/34 and the
  BC release pages linked there. Store them in `src/bodycombat/catalog.js`.
- Do not copy choreography write-ups from that site into the app.
- Placeholder ratings are integers 1–5. Durations are estimates, labeled as
  such in the UI, and must stay editable.
- User edits live in localStorage only (`metaStore.js`).

## Class shape

- 60 minutes: tracks 1A, 1B, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10 in order. A single
  track 1 can stand in for 1A+1B. Track 5 may be one song or 5A then 5B.
- 45 minutes: tracks 1–7 in order, then exactly one of track 8, 9, or 10.
- 30 minutes: warmup, track 2, track 3, track 7, then track 9 or 10 (5–6 songs).

## Testing

- Keep unit tests in `test/bodycombat/` and run them with `node --test`.
- `buildProgram.js` stays free of DOM and `localStorage` so the tests can call it directly.
